# Backend API Standards

- Keep views thin; move business logic into services/selectors/repositories.
- Do not place domain logic in Django signals.
- Avoid over-abstraction; prefer clear, direct code over premature generic layers.
- Never use silent exception handling (`except: pass` or swallowed errors).
- Keep function bodies under 40 lines; split into focused helpers when needed.
- Enforce formatting/linting with `black`, `isort`, and `flake8`.
- Use pagination for every list API endpoint.
- Return consistent API payloads with success, message, data, errors, and meta.
- Avoid `.all()` in production API query paths; always filter intentionally.
- Use `select_related` / `prefetch_related` for relational API reads.
- Ensure audit fields (`created_at`, `updated_at`, `created_by`, `updated_by`) on new business tables.
- Add indexes for high-cardinality filters: foreign keys, status, and date fields.
- Keep heavy operations async (Celery/background jobs), not request-thread blocking.
- Monitor API latency and target p95 under 300ms.
- Use structured logs and keep error tracking enabled in non-local environments.
- Include manual architecture review as part of substantial backend changes.
